To determine the efficiency of the method, a
recovery study was carried out. This was done by
spiking a known concentration (0.5 mg/g) of one
of the metals of interest into one of the fruit
samples prior to digestion and the sample was
subjected to all the pretreatment step as other
samples and analyzed using AS after
pretreatment and digestion. The percentage
recovery was calculated using the following
